One night two men from Egulac went down to the river for a swim. They were Egush and Eganada. They swam and they swam and they swam. Finally Egush said to Eganada, "Do you know what I think?" Eganada said, "No, what do you think?" Egush said, "I think the Great Spirit gave us too much water." Eganada said, "Why do you think that?" Egush said, "Because we are getting ready to drown." They swam and they swam and they swam. Finally Eganada said, "Do you know what I think?" Egush said, "No, what do you think?" Eganada said, "I think the Great Spirit is testing us." They swam and they swam and they swam. Finally they reached the shore and they were very tired. They lay down and rested. Then Egush said to Eganada, "Do you know what I think?" Eganada said, "No, what do you think?" Egush said, "I think the Great Spirit is happy with us." They got up and went back to their village. As they approached, they saw that everything was destroyed. Their houses, their fields, their cattle were gone. And they knew that this was the punishment of the Great Spirit. And they lived happily ever after.

